- Add: Set the PostgreSQL connection application_name to fda for pooled and direct connections (visible in pg_stat_activity)
- Add: PUT FDA action now can take a body to update some FDA parameters (#196)
- Fix: PUT FDA without a body on an uploaded FDA now returns 409 `FDAUploadNotRegenerable` and properly releases the PostgreSQL client
- Add: DuckDB memory usage in the Fetcher heartbeat (now `INFO`), in an `INFO` dump of `duckdb_memory()` before every Parquet export and in the memory peak sampled during it (`INFO` on success, `WARN` on failure, interval set with `FDA_DUCKDB_MEMORY_SAMPLE_INTERVAL_MS`, default `250`), in `GET /health` (`duckdb` block) and as Prometheus gauges (`fda_duckdb_*`) to diagnose Out of Memory errors; `INFO` log when the temporary Parquet files of an FDA are cleaned, after a failed fetch or on deletion (#351)
- Add: `FDA_DUCKDB_S3_UPLOADER_MAX_FILESIZE` (default `50GB`) and `FDA_DUCKDB_PARTITIONED_WRITE_MAX_OPEN_FILES` (default `8`) to reduce the non-spillable `httpfs` upload memory of partitioned Parquet exports, which caused Out of Memory errors (#355)
- Fix: a refresh removes the files of the partitions it rewrites that the new export did not write again, so a partition written as several files no longer keeps stale rows (#355)
- Add: `FDA_DUCKDB_SORT_PARTITIONED_EXPORTS` (default `true`) sorts the rows of partitioned Parquet exports by `timeColumn` so each partition is written in as few files as possible; the sort may spill to `FDA_DUCKDB_TEMP_DIR` (#355)
- Add: logs about remove duckdb tmp files (size and number)
- Add: optional lifetime download quotas and expiration dates/validity periods for public FDA links, enforced atomically across instances, with remaining-download metadata and HTTP 410 rejection after expiration or exhaustion (#338)
- Add: persisted FDA resource accounting: creation time, Parquet storage measurements, buffered FDA/DA query counters, queries since the last successful refresh and refresh cost. Expose service/servicePath accounting through GET /usage and Prometheus gauges. Configure the access-counter flush interval with `FDA_ACCESS_FLUSH_INTERVAL_MS` (default `10000`). (#324)
- Add: a fetch that exceeds the MinIO bucket quota now ends `failed` with an explicit `StorageQuotaExceeded` error (HTTP 507), and the quota is documented for operators (#325)
- Add: `lazy` field on FDA creation. A lazy FDA is created `idle`: it is not fetched and no refresh is scheduled until its first query, which waits for the fetch. Then it follows its refresh policy (`none`, `interval` or `window`) (#326)
- Add: `onDemand` refresh policy (`maxAge`), a cache that is fetched on the first query and only refreshed when a query finds it older than `maxAge`. Partitioned onDemand FDAs refresh incrementally from the partition of the last fetch and can keep a window (`windowSize`). Concurrent queries share a single fetch (#326)
- Add: `FDA_ON_DEMAND_WAIT_TIMEOUT_MS` (default `30000`), `FDA_ON_DEMAND_POLL_INTERVAL_MS` (default `500`) and `FDA_ON_DEMAND_RETRY_BACKOFF_MS` (default `60000`) env vars to configure how queries wait for lazy and onDemand fetches (#326)
- Upgrade: PostGIS image from `postgis/postgis:15-3.3` to `postgis/postgis:16-3.4` (docker-compose and integration tests). Existing `docker/postgis-data` volumes created with PostgreSQL 15 must be recreated or migrated (#334)
- Upgrade: MinIO client image in docker-compose replaced from `minio/mc` to `pgsty/mc` (#302)
- Fix: recurring FDA refresh consistency check to use the Agenda 6 API, restoring detection of active consistency refreshes and preventing agenda.jobs is not a function warnings (introduced in 1.7.0 version) (#346)
- Fix: a failed fetch removes its staging CSV, and non partitioned FDAs publish through `tmp/`, so a failed refresh keeps the last good data (#325)
- Fix: a failed PostgreSQL upload no longer returns its half-closed connection to the pool, which could hang the next fetch (#325)
- Add: optional `timeRange` field in DAs (declared by default in `defaultDataAccess`) so queries by time range on partitioned FDAs read only the partitions overlapping the range instead of all of them (#328)
- Fix: Mongo `find` FDAs with `refreshPolicy.type=window` now reject (400) a `timeColumn` that is an alias in the `projection`, which made the FDA complete with no rows; it must be a raw field projected with `1` or `true` (#363)
